# The Physics of UI Motion

Linear transitions look mechanical and robotic. Natural interfaces use **spring damping** or **ease-out** curves:

```css
/* Entering elements: Fast enter, smooth decelerate */
transition: transform 250ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);

/* Exiting elements: Accelerate out */
transition: opacity 150ms cubic-bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0);
```

# Go Concurrency Primitives

```go
func Worker(ctx context.Context, jobs <-chan int, results chan<- int) {
    for {
        select {
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return
        case job, ok := <-jobs:
            if !ok { return }
            results <- job * 2
        }
    }
}
```

# Idempotent Queued Jobs in Laravel

To prevent race conditions during high concurrency, utilize atomic cache locks:

```php
public function handle(): void
{
    Redis::funnel('process-order:'.$this->orderId)
        ->limit(1)
